@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# Memory review: patched 1.6.1 versus patched 2.0.0
+
+The archived 1.6.1 patch stack was replayed from its pinned commit
+9914146eeae7b46b300f475a16c32426fc02ec1f. This is a source comparison,
+not an on-device before/after RAM benchmark.
+
+| Area | 1.6.1 | 2.0.0 / correction |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Quote sharing | 12 KiB worker stack, HTTP cleanup, Wi-Fi shutdown, durable SD outbox | Same mechanism before this fix; no newly introduced share-worker leak established. Release failure-path job payloads before announcing completion. |
+| TLS | HTTP client uses framework TLS allocator | Current X4 Pro framework selects internal-memory TLS. Fixed 512-byte HTTP streaming buffers and critical-starvation checks keep unsafe shares queued. Normal post-Wi-Fi heap shapes proceed to the fallible HTTP/TLS client; the earlier speculative 112 KiB/32 KiB threshold was too strict. |
+| Share JSON | Child-list JSON in PSRAM; other documents on default heap | All sharing JSON documents now explicitly use PSRAM. Failed metadata serialization is rejected before publishing a job. |
+| Compressed fonts | Allocate/free inflate scratch per group | 2.0 reuses one call-local scratch buffer, reducing allocation churn. Pixel payloads, hot group and scratch now prefer PSRAM, with the existing default fallback on non-PSRAM devices. |
+| Dictionary rendering | Prewarm scope ends before word overlay | Same lifetime bug persisted in 2.0; now survives through overlay drawing. Regression test uses the actual render block. This does not prove it was the sole cause of the reported corruption. |
+| Scalable fonts | Bounded PSRAM workspace and pixel arena | Same capacity constants; new implementation adds bounded cache admission and inactive-font release. No reason found to halve these arenas indiscriminately. |
+| Highlight geometry | Reserves metadata for 10,000 words up front | Short auto-highlights now reserve only their known word count; other selections start at 512 and grow with heap checks. The 10,000-word limit remains. |
+| Diagnostics | Serial heap figures | Optional, allocation-free RAM icon and percentage in the configurable status row. On-demand pool totals, largest free block, ten smallest task stack headrooms. No polling worker or periodic e-ink refresh. |
+
+The current SDK does not enable per-task heap allocation tracking. Task stack
+headroom is minimum free stack, **not total RAM consumption**, and is labelled
+accordingly. Task numbers are copied from the scheduler snapshot; task-name
+pointers are deliberately not dereferenced after a worker may have exited.
+
+## Hardware verification
+
+On X4 Pro, record the RAM indicator and `share.start`/`share.cleaned` serial
+pool snapshots. Repeatedly share a quote, wait for Wi-Fi to disappear, then
+look up words, including selecting words inside dictionary definitions.
+Expect legible fonts, no monotonic heap loss, no heap-integrity errors, and
+queued shares preserved if internal RAM cannot admit TLS. A first network
+connection may initialize shared framework infrastructure; distinguish that
+one-time change from a leak growing on every share. No cache reset is needed.
+
+Test new and existing highlight endpoint drags at both screen edges, in both
+orientations. Brief contact gaps must not save early; deliberate edge dwell
+must turn one page without skipping pages while the finger is stationary.
+
+## Arabic dictionary follow-up
+
+A different Arabic dictionary font must be restored after painting the Latin
+reader background. Bitmap-font admission now permits PSRAM-backed loading
+without demanding an unrelated 32 KiB internal block, while retaining internal
+headroom checks. Definition rendering prewarms scalable fonts as well as
+bitmap SD fonts, detects an Arabic page backed by a Latin-only family, and
+tries one clean reload of the requested family. Failures no longer silently
+show replacement boxes; a retry is available, and one automatic retry follows
+completion of an overlapping quote share. The activity owns its font-family
+name and its lookup controller borrows the activity-owned cache path.
+
+Regression tests reproduce the Latin-only Arabic fallback using real Arabic
+shaping, exercise successful/failed family reload and one-shot post-share
+retry, and cover fragmented internal RAM with and without PSRAM. They do not
+replace testing the user's installed Arabic font and SD card on hardware.
